2026-09-03T11:03Z Minh Ha-Duong created

2026-09-03T11:13Z claude note measured: forced-mean against the committed cls cells at fp32 on the 0266 cross-lingual set. granite-97m -27,5% MRR and -34,6% hit@1, gte-multilingual-base -12,7% and -10,3%, arctic-embed-m-v2 -10,3% and -14,7%. Positive control first: the patched driver re-ran gte's committed cls cell field-for-field identical, which is what licenses reusing the committed cells as control arms. For gte and granite the forced arm IS upstream's shipped configuration (empty template, no e5 segment in the id), so the number is not a hypothetical. Second finding, and the one that settles the remedy: 1_Pooling/config.json is absent from the four ONNX mirrors the docs point users at (Xenova/*, onnx-community/*) and present only on the two originals, so the correct pooling cannot be auto-detected from the repo the code loads -- it has to be curated, which is the registry entry. Report at verification/POOLING-DEFECT-0612.md, filing draft at verification/UPSTREAM-ISSUE-POOLING-0612.md, cells under bench/results/0612-pooling-ablation/
2026-09-03T11:30Z claude note upstream moved twice during the session and struck half the framing: at 13:18 he shipped ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_DTYPE with the precision in the identity (230183d, merged b0e0bc8), which is Michael's quantized ask delivered and the knob 0220 withdrew, done soundly. Re-verified at b0e0bc8: dtype now appears 15 times in embeddings.ts, and pooling: 'mean' is still the single occurrence in the whole src tree. So the measurement stands and is sharper -- prefixes inferred, dtype in the identity, pooling the last axis written at the call site. Report and draft corrected before anything went out; the outward vehicle is now a PR rather than an issue on the author's ruling, staged pooling-first, and the rebuild onto b0e0bc8 is underway
2026-09-03T11:40Z claude note author ruling: ship ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_POOLING as the override, with the curated table under it. Two corrections to my reading. First, the 2026-08-29 no-knob ruling targeted a STANDALONE precision knob on the ground that precision cannot travel alone; it does not forbid a knob once the thing it travels with exists, and model/prefixes/dtype are all settable now. Second, the shape to copy is the maintainer's own: ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_PREFIXES is an escape hatch on an id inference, and the pooling equivalent is an escape hatch on a curated table -- same architecture, different oracle, because for pooling an inference is impossible (the mirror probe). A knob alone would not repair the user it is for: someone who picks gte-multilingual-base on the docs' invitation cannot learn it wants cls, so the table fixes the default and the variable covers the mirrored or renamed checkpoint. Report and draft PR body aligned; the override carries no weight in the embedder identity, where PREFIXES also sits
--- body ---

## Context

Upstream closed issue #43 on 2026-09-03 by shipping local model selection:
`ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL` now reaches the local provider as a raw Hugging Face
id, E5 prefixes are applied by a regex on that id, and the embedder identity
becomes `local:<model>`. Verified at upstream HEAD `76bbb07`.

Two vector-affecting properties did not travel with it. `embeddings.ts` still
calls `extractor(input, { pooling: 'mean', normalize: true })` for every model,
and `dtype` does not appear in the file at all. The maintainer named the second
himself, as the precondition for the quantized build Michael-Logies asked for
in the same thread: dtype must be in the embedder identity, "otherwise an index
re-embedded at another precision is indistinguishable from one that was not."

The same sentence is true of pooling one axis over, and pooling is worse than
dtype in one respect: nothing about it is user-visible. In this repository's
own measured registry, 11 of 23 entries declare a pooling other than `mean` —
10 `cls`, one `last_token`. `mean` is correct for exactly the one model it was
written for, the incumbent MiniLM, which is why nothing has noticed. The knob
shipped today is what makes it reachable for the rest.

Ticket 0421 established the class from the model cards. Nobody had measured
what it costs, and a maintainer reading "your code applies the wrong pooling"
is entitled to ask.

## Relevant files

- `bench/cross_lingual_probe.mjs` — the 0266 driver; gains `--force-pooling`
- `bench/cross_lingual_score.py` — carries the ablation markers into the score
- `bench/models.json` — the declared pooling and its per-model provenance
- `verification/POOLING-DEFECT-0612.md` — the report this ticket produces
- `~/data/projets/zoteus-bench/0266-pooling/` — the vectors and score cells

## Actions

1. Give the 0266 probe a `--force-pooling` arm that runs the wrong pooling on
   purpose, marked in the manifest and the score so an ablation cell can never
   be read as a measurement of the model.
2. Re-run one committed cell unchanged as a positive control: the patched
   driver must reproduce it exactly before any delta is believed.
3. Measure the forced-`mean` arm at fp32 against the committed `cls` arm for
   every `cls` candidate already cached.
4. Establish whether the correct value is auto-detectable from the repository
   the code loads, or whether it must be curated.
5. Write the report and the upstream filing; the registry entry is the remedy,
   and it is the same object that carries the dtype Michael needs.

## Test

- The positive control is the red-first step: the re-run of an untouched cell
  must be field-for-field identical to the committed one. A driver that fails
  this cannot support any conclusion drawn from the ablation arms.

## Verification

- [x] `--force-pooling` rejects a mode the drivers cannot pass
- [x] An ablation cell records `declared_pooling` and `pooling_forced`
- [x] The control re-run reproduces the committed cell exactly
- [x] Each `cls` candidate measured at fp32, both arms
- [x] The auto-detection question answered against the actual mirrors

## Invariants

- The two arms differ in pooling and nothing else — same driver, same corpus,
  same dtype, same template, one flag.
- No ablation cell is written where an ordinary cell is read from.
- `bench/models.json` is unchanged: this ticket measures the defect, it does
  not re-declare anything.

## Exit criteria

- The cost of upstream's hardcoded `mean` is a measured number on at least two
  `cls` models, with the positive control recorded beside it.
- The report says plainly whether pooling can be read from the loaded repo.
- The upstream filing is drafted, shown to the author, and filed or deferred
  with the reason recorded here.
